        "comments": "The cobiont assembly jmKudNeot1 is based on PacBio HiFi data and Arima Hi-C data generated at the Wellcome Sanger Institute for fThuAlb1. The assembly process included the following sequence of steps: Initial PacBio assembly with hifiasm-meta and Hi-C based scaffolding with YaHs. Host fish scaffolds were identified and removed based on scaffold tetranucleotide composition (https://github.com/CobiontID/read_VAE/tree/main/contig_tools), chromatin interaction network clusters (https://github.com/CobiontID/HiC_network), and mapping against the released fThuAlb1 assembly. Retained haplotypic duplication was then removed with purge_dups. A circular mitochondrial contig was identified in the meta-assembly.",
